    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#12', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#12', 'display', 'Guide', 'Follow the numbered buttons above the tabs for a new story. Tabs stay freely accessible; the buttons navigate without applying or starting a story.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_all', 'Read whole guide', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_stop_speech', 'Stop guide speech', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#13', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#13', 'display', 'Guide', '1. Create story: in Master, write a rough premise and choose Cast generation settings. Choose a provider/model. Refine story idea fills the fields; Refine & build complete draft also generates the cast, scenes and lore.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#14', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#14', 'display', 'Guide', '2. Scenes & lore (optional): review generated scenes and facts, or add your own. A clean editor loads the new draft automatically; unsent edits are preserved. Send to Master Draft after editing.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#15', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#15', 'display', 'Guide', '3. Apply story: review the Master draft and cast options, then Apply Draft to activate and save it. Clean-start story memory on apply can clear the current story memory.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#16', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#16', 'display', 'Guide', '4. Voices & media (optional): review each persona in Voice, Story Images and Story Sounds. Configure only the media you want.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#17', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#17', 'display', 'Guide', '5. Check setup: open Story Health and press Check Story Setup. Use repair controls for missing narrator, voices, images or sounds.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#18', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#18', 'display', 'Guide', '6. Play: press Start Play, then send a player action or Continue to request narration. Ordinary stories do not request a model reply from Start Play alone; authored scenarios may narrate their opening.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#19', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#19', 'display', 'Guide', 'Returning to a story: Continue current story opens Play. Loading a saved story is available in Master. Neither navigation button regenerates a draft.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#20', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#20', 'display', 'Guide', 'Direct access: Registry and Editor manage characters; Session and AR expose detailed state. All tabs remain available at every step.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#21', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#21', 'display', 'Guide', 'Troubleshooting: use Story Health to preview the next request or explain routing; inspect detailed output in Troubleshooting.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#22', 'unnamed_qlabel_qlabel#22', 'display', 'Guide', '10. Use Story Library Export below the Story Library card when a story is ready to move, share, or back up as a zip package with selectable sections. Green rows mean data exists; selected avatar, voice, and AudioFX files are copied into the package.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_quick_start', 'Read Quick Start', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qplaintextedit_qplaintextedit', 'QPlainTextEdit', 'multiline', 'Guide', 'The Story Health tab is the local story readiness view. Use it whenever you want confidence that AR is ready before pressing Continue.\n\nWhat it gives you:\n- Load Demo if Needed & Check: loads the demo only if no story is active, then checks setup. Use the separate voice, image and sound tests; start narration from Play.\n- Built-in templates: fantasy mystery, sci-fi horror, and cozy tavern adventure.\n- Story Health: active story, AR on/off, story-owned narrator, active personas, memory, voices, visuals, and story sounds.\n- Check Story Setup: readable setup checks in the UI, not only logs.\n- Repair buttons: choose narrator, browse voice file, disable missing story sounds, fix image path, create memory snapshot, relink personas, and reset invalid overrides.\n- Voice Routing Check: shows exactly how [NARRATOR] and [CHARACTER: Name] route to personas and voice files.\n- Next-turn inspector: preview the next AR request or explain narrator, character, voice, memory, Visual Reply, and AudioFX routing.\n- Story Memory: pin facts, review recent memory, delete one memory, reset character memory, or reset story memory.\n- Story Bundle export/import: compact JSON bundle for story setup, cast, narrator setup, memory, prompts, AudioFX, visuals, and routing.\n- Story Library Export in the Master tab: zip package export/import below Story Library, with selectable sections, green availability rows, copied avatar/voice/audio assets, and safe import remapping.\n\nIf something does not happen, check Setup Checks and What Needs Attention before changing prompts.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_story_health', 'Read Story Health', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qplaintextedit_qplaintextedit#2', 'QPlainTextEdit', 'multiline', 'Guide', 'AR mode is the story-first mode for MPRC. It is meant for cinematic interactive adventures rather than normal assistant chat or equal-turn group chat.\n\nWhat AR changes:\n- The narrator leads the scene and only brings in characters when they are relevant.\n- Personas can use their AR description and AR system prompt instead of their normal companion prompt.\n- The prompt keeps compact state: current scene, location, mood, story goal, active characters, recent events, and pending choices.\n- Replies may include structured sections like [NARRATOR], [CHARACTER: Name], [AMBIENCE: pub ambient], [MUSIC: adventure music], [FX: magic shimmer], [STINGER: danger stinger], and [CHOICES].\n- Audio tags are not spoken by TTS. They trigger matching AudioFX files in the background when Story Sounds is enabled.\n- Story Sounds can use the AudioFX database so the model knows which local sound cues are available.\n- Character labels such as [CHARACTER: Name] are used for per-persona voice routing when the persona has a valid voice sample.\n\nGood AR setup:\n1. Enable AlternativeReality Mode.\n2. Keep Use AR persona prompts enabled.\n3. Fill AR descriptions for characters that need a different story identity.\n4. Set pacing to Slow / Audiobook for longer narration, or Balanced for more frequent user choices.\n5. Add story sound files in the Story Sounds tab if you want ambience cues to play during the story.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_alternativereality_mode', 'Read AlternativeReality Mode', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qplaintextedit_qplaintextedit#3', 'QPlainTextEdit', 'multiline', 'Guide', "Master prepares a reusable story setup. Refinement, generation and applying are separate actions.\n\n1. Enter a rough premise in Story prompt. Keep important names, species, relationships and the central conflict.\n2. Review Mode, SFW and Cast generation. Native story personas to draft is the requested profile count; Maximum created characters is a separate limit for Apply Draft.\n3. Choose a Refinement provider. Current main model follows NC's current chat selection. For another configured provider, load its models or enter a model ID. This selection applies to both refinement actions and all complete-draft stages.\n4. Refine story idea proposes a detailed campaign brief, cast plan, opening scene title, location, time, mood and avatar visual direction. Successful results fill the input fields automatically. Check Preview only to review before accepting. Mode, SFW and cast settings remain your choices.\n5. Refine & build complete draft runs three stages with the selected model: brief, Master draft and cast, then related scenes and lore. Watch the progress indicator; Retry failed stage resumes completed work. The separate Generate Story Setup uses the current main model. Neither action activates the story.\n6. Optionally edit Scenarios & Lore. A clean editor loads the latest draft automatically. Unsent edits are preserved; Reload Master Draft replaces them only after confirmation. Send to Master Draft copies your authored changes back.\n7. Review the draft and Cast generation settings, then Apply Draft. In the native interface this activates and saves the draft directly. Enable or disable persona creation, existing-persona updates, voice assignment, avatar creation and clean-start memory before applying.\n8. Check voices and optional images/sounds, run Story Health checks, then Play.\n\nCast count zero asks only for characters explicitly required by your premise. A positive count must match the refinement cast plan. A conflict or malformed response leaves your current fields unchanged. Changing fields, cast settings or the current main model invalidates an older preview.\n\nRefinement can be cancelled or discarded. It never executes scenario actions. Accepted text remains editable before Generate Story Setup.\n\nSave Story preserves the draft in the library. Clear / Restart Story clears current Master story state and links; saved personas and story files remain. Story Library Export creates portable packages including the selected local assets.", (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_master_story_builder', 'Read Master Story Builder', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qplaintextedit_qplaintextedit#4', 'QPlainTextEdit', 'multiline', 'Guide', 'The Story Images tab controls real story-scene images sent to the existing Visual Reply window. It is separate from the current-character preview panel.\n\nRecommended workflow:\n1. Select a persona, then enable story images in Visual Reply for that persona.\n2. Choose When to generate. Good first choices are When user asks for image, Important story moments, AR story beats, or When choices appear. Every assistant reply is useful for testing but can generate too many images with paid providers.\n3. Fill Character visual description, clothing / props, and environment style so the scene prompt keeps identity and setting consistent.\n4. Keep Use latest scene summary and Include active speaker enabled when you want images to show what is happening in the story instead of only a portrait.\n5. Use Preview Image Prompt before generating. Use Generate Visual Reply for a manual test. Auto requests still respect cooldown and max auto images per session.\n\nProvider prompt styles:\n- Grok/xAI: richer natural-language prompt with current story moment, visible action, persona identity, appearance, scene, mood, lighting, style, and continuity.\n- Runware: shorter direct prompt with concrete subject, action, location, style, lighting/mood, and continuity terms. This avoids overloading Runware with long story instructions.\n- ComfyUI: compact direct positive prompt, preserving the existing ComfyUI behavior.\n\nIf images do not appear, check that Visual Reply itself has a configured provider, this persona has visual generation enabled, the trigger mode matches the scene, cooldown has expired, and max auto images/session has not been reached.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_visual_reply_story_images', 'Read Visual Reply Story Images', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qplaintextedit_qplaintextedit#5', 'QPlainTextEdit', 'multiline', 'Guide', 'The Story Sounds tab controls the sounds a story can actually play. It has two related jobs: build/save sound descriptions, and connect those descriptions to real local audio files.\n\nRecommended workflow:\n1. Open Story Sounds and keep Story Sounds enabled.\n2. Click Import Audio Pack Resources and choose a prepared pack folder such as Q:\\Sounds. The folder should contain mprc_audio_pack.json or audio_pack.json.\n3. Set story sound volume low enough that background sounds do not overpower TTS. This affects automatic story sounds and manual previews only.\n4. Check the Story Sound Library. Green items are ready: the local file exists and is indexed for story use.\n5. Use Play Sound to preview a selected cue, or Play [AMBIENCE: pub ambient] to test tag playback.\n6. In AR stories, the model should choose from available AudioFX descriptions and write exact tags such as [AMBIENCE: pub ambient], [MUSIC: adventure music], [FX: magic shimmer], or [STINGER: danger stinger].\n7. When a matching tag appears in chat, MPRC removes that tag before TTS and plays the matching file in the background.\n\nImportant rules:\n- The model should not invent sound names. It should choose descriptions that exist in the Story Sound Library.\n- [AMBIENCE: ...] is for background environments, [MUSIC: ...] is for music, [FX: ...] is for short effects, and [STINGER: ...] is for brief dramatic hits.\n- Imported sound packs only store file paths in addon settings. Removing an AudioFX item does not delete the sound file from disk.\n- If a tag is spoken aloud, either Story Sounds is off, the cue was not matched, or the tag reached TTS before the audio scanner saw a complete bracketed tag.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_audio_tab_and_story_sounds', 'Read Audio Tab And Story Sounds', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qplaintextedit_qplaintextedit#6', 'QPlainTextEdit', 'multiline', 'Guide', 'Master: create or refine a premise, generate a draft, apply, save or load stories.\nScenarios & Lore: optional scenes, facts, conditions, choices and current-main-model refinement.\nRegistry: add, duplicate, import, export and select personas.\nEditor: edit persona descriptions, AR profiles, prompts and pictures.\nVoice: review character voice samples and backend support.\nStory Images: per-persona Visual Reply behavior, previews and generation limits.\nStory Sounds: sound descriptions and local audio files used by story tags.\nStory Health: setup checks, templates, repairs, voice routing, memory and bundles.\nPlay: story feed, player actions, speech, choices and image triggers.\nSession: detailed scene and roster state.\nAR: AlternativeReality pacing, characters, goals and choices.\nGuide: instructions for this workflow.\nTroubleshooting: effective prompts, voice routing and diagnostics.\nStatus: additional addon controls and status.\n\nNumbered navigation is optional. Visiting a tab never marks its setup complete.', (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_which_tab_to_use', 'Read Which Tab To Use', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qplaintextedit_qplaintextedit#7', 'QPlainTextEdit', 'multiline', 'Guide', "Image not generating: open Visual Reply itself and confirm provider, model, API key/base URL, and image size. Then check this persona's Story Images tab: enabled, trigger mode, cooldown, and max auto images.\n\nRunware image quality drops: use Preview Image Prompt and keep the prompt compact. Runware usually works better with direct concrete visual phrases than with long story instructions.\n\nGrok/xAI image is too plain: add richer character appearance, clothing/props, scene, mood, lighting, and style details. Grok/xAI handles natural-language prompts better than Runware.\n\nVoice not applying: newly created personas need a voice sample path in the Voice tab, and the active NC TTS backend must support reference audio. Unsupported backends keep speaking with the normal voice.\n\nVoice changes during one response: check Troubleshooting or Story Health -> Voice Routing Check. A voice should switch only on explicit [NARRATOR], [CHARACTER: Exact Persona Display Name], or supported speaker labels; plain AR narration should stay on the narrator.\n\nNarrator/persona mismatch: choose the narrator explicitly in Story Health or Voice, then validate. The inspector shows route reasons such as explicit_persona, text_speaker_label, ar_narrator_default, ar_stream_speaker, current_speaker, or active_persona.", (), True, False, {}),
    ('mprc_guide_read_troubleshooting', 'Read Troubleshooting', 'action', 'Guide', None, (), False, False, {}),
    ('unnamed_qplaintextedit_qplaintextedit#8', 'QPlainTextEdit', 'multiline', 'Guide', 'The Lantern Archive\n\nMode: Narrator + characters\nLocation: A quiet archive workshop with a planning table, map wall, voice recorder, and image board.\nMood: Curious, focused, collaborative\nObjective: Use the full persona roster to plan a small mystery scene, explain choices clearly, and generate story images when useful.\n\nPersona roster:\n- Mentor: guides setup and explains options.\n- Friend: keeps the session relaxed and easy to continue.\n- Story Narrator: describes scene beats and atmosphere.\n- Game Master: tracks choices, objectives, and consequences.\n- Custom Character Template: ready for the user to reshape.', (), True, False, {}),
